From 32bef845a1350918205a4cff6c2e99fef1be3ce0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cylewitruk <cyle.witruk@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:43:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the moment a request reached the server by its
 application data

The mark is taken when the last application data of a prefix has been
written to the server, not when it was read from the prover, and is not
moved by other records such as the alert answering a close. It is given
as a position in the received stream, so that it holds whatever the
prefix covers, and the tap tells how much application data had begun to
arrive by a position.
---
 crates/tlsn/src/proxy.rs    | 148 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 crates/tlsn/src/verifier.rs |   4 +-
 2 files changed, 127 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

